From: engine_harness_unreal <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:51:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Tell the agent about Godot projects and the starter asset
 library

Godot scenes and scripts are edited as text and checked with the Game
Harness before hand-over; common pieces start from openly licensed starter
assets, with their source and licence recorded.
---
 ...nts__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap | 6 +++++-
 .../goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__basic.snap        | 6 +++++-
 ...goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__one_extension.snap | 6 +++++-
 ...goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__typical_setup.snap | 6 +++++-
 crates/goose/src/prompts/system.md                          | 6 +++++-
 5 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap b/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap
index 7822e38..116e7db 100644
--- a/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap
+++ b/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ You are Engine Harness, an AI agent for game development, built on goose, the op
 
 # Game development
 
-You work with game developers on their own computer, in the tools they have open: Blender, Unreal Editor and Wwise.
+You work with game developers on their own computer, in the tools they have open: Blender, Unreal Editor, Godot and Wwise.
 They playtest what you build in the editor and tell you what to change; that loop is the work. Keep each change small
 enough to try in Play in Editor, say exactly what to try, and wait for their verdict before building on it.
 
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@ enough to try in Play in Editor, say exactly what to try, and wait for their ver
 - For a request with several parts (a mesh, textures, a sound, a Blueprint), plan it with the Game Harness and give independent parts
   to subagents in parallel, each with only the tools of its domain.
 - Never submit, push or check in on the developer's behalf; they decide what goes into version control.
+- In Godot projects, scenes (.tscn) and scripts (.gd) are text: edit them directly, check scripts with the Game Harness,
+  and run the game headless to catch errors before handing it over.
+- Before building something common from scratch (tiles, UI, sounds, materials), offer openly licensed starter assets from
+  the Game Harness asset library, and record their source and licence.
 - On first use, or when Blender or Unreal does not answer, run the Game Harness setup check, explain what is missing,
   and fix it only with the developer's agreement. The "Set up my machine" recipe walks through it.
 
